=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: false
faulty_devices: none
diagnosis_text:
No fault exists in the lab. A thorough end-to-end investigation found the
entire Kath2 topology operating normally. Every Office LAN host
(office_pc, enquiry, exam_cell, tpo — all on 192.168.3.0/24) can
successfully reach both the Server Room subnet (1.0.0.0/8, represented by
pc1 at 1.0.0.5) and the Internet Lab subnet (128.168.0.0/16, represented by
pc2–pc5) with zero packet loss. All three routers carry complete RIP routing
tables: router1 holds RIP-learned routes to 1.0.0.0/8 and 128.168.0.0/16 via
its eth3 WAN link to router2 (20.20.0.1→20.20.0.2), while router2
holds return routes to 192.168.3.0/24 via that same link. RIP on router1 shows
two active, error-free neighbours (router0 at 10.10.0.1 and router2 at
20.20.0.2, both updated within the last 30 seconds). All physical interfaces
on router0, router1, and router2 are UP with correct IP assignments. All
Office-LAN end-hosts are configured with the correct default gateway
(192.168.3.1, router1 eth0), and all Server Room / Internet Lab hosts point
correctly to router2 (1.0.0.1 and 128.168.0.1 respectively). The ticket
describes a problem that does not exist in the current lab state — this is a
false-premise report. No device restart is required; the helpdesk ticket
should be closed as "no fault found / unable to reproduce."
=== END ===
